#!/command/with-contenv sh
# shellcheck shell=sh
# When the reporter is switched off, run exits 0 and we return 125 —
# s6-supervise's "permanent failure, do not restart" marker — so the slot
# reports down instead of spinning.
#
# When it IS switched on we deliberately do NOT return 125: a reporter that
# died should come back. The dashboard service returns 125 unconditionally,
# which is right for a UI you can see is missing and wrong for a background
# job whose absence is silent.
case "${AGENT_INDEX:-}" in
    1|true|TRUE|True|yes|YES|Yes) exit 0 ;;
    *) exit 125 ;;
esac
